output/
*.xlsx
service-account.json
oauth-token.json
ownerville-creds.json
# ...and their timestamped BACKUPS. The bare names above were ignored but
# `ownerville-creds.json.bak.20260802-230835` was not, so a rotated credential
# sat untracked in the root of a PUBLIC repo, one `git add .` from being
# published (found 2026-08-12). Cover every secret-file backup, not just this one.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*-creds.json*
*-token.json*
brand-audit-keys.json
vantura-payroll-webapp.json
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.DS_Store
# Browser profiles — all variants (.browser_profile, _holder, _zoho, …) hold
# live session cookies (auth). Sensitive; never commit.
.browser_profile*
# Wildcard on purpose: the multi-account capture (0c8def6) mints a NEW profile
# and state file per account (.appstream_profile_cap_<name>,
# .appstream_storage_state_<name>.json) — a per-name list here would leak the
# next account added. Also covers the .launchlock siblings.
.appstream_profile*
# The THROWAWAY ownerville login-test profile (tableau_patchright
# --ownerville-form-login). A sibling of .browser_profile, so the wildcard above
# does NOT catch it: it sat untracked on Lucy 1 as the runner's only "locally
# modified" entry (2026-08-26). Same reason as .saraplus_profile below — a
# browser profile carrying a live OV login attempt, in a PUBLIC repo, one
# `git add .` from being published.
automations/uploaded/.ov_login_test/
# The DEDICATED resume-extract Chrome profile + its cache (resume_pushing/run.py:
# APPSTREAM_PROFILE_DIR.parent / ".extract_profile" / ".extractor_cache"). Same
# story as .ov_login_test right above: siblings of .browser_profile, so the
# wildcard misses them, and they are a REAL Chrome profile — Default/Extensions,
# driven over CDP against AppStream/Indeed — so they carry live login state in a
# PUBLIC repo. Found untracked on Lucy 2 as its only two "locally modified"
# entries (2026-08-27). Regenerated on every run; nothing to commit, and an
# untracked directory here is also what silently aborts a `git pull` the day
# anything upstream lands at the same path.
automations/uploaded/.extract_profile/
automations/uploaded/.extractor_cache/
# AppStream storage_state export — contains live SESSION cookies (auth). Sensitive;
# never commit. Exported by output/_scratch_appstream_export_state.py.
.appstream_storage_state*.json
automations/shared/.appstream_storage_state*.json
# ownerville storage_state export — contains live SESSION cookies (auth). Sensitive;
# never commit. Exported by output/_scratch_ownerville_export_state.py.
.ownerville_storage_state.json
automations/shared/.ownerville_storage_state.json
# Credico storage_state export — contains live SESSION cookies (auth). Sensitive;
# the repo is PUBLIC. Never commit.
.credico_storage_state.json
automations/shared/.credico_storage_state.json
output/_credico_profile/
# Sara Plus scrape (b2b_sales_board) — the browser profile and the storage_state
# both hold Carlos's live SESSION cookies (auth). The repo is PUBLIC, and 661
# profile files were sitting untracked one `git add .` away. Never commit.
.saraplus_profile/
automations/b2b_sales_board/.saraplus_profile/
.saraplus_storage_state.json
automations/b2b_sales_board/.saraplus_storage_state.json
# Probe screenshots — throwaway debug captures written beside the _probe_*.py
# scripts (ignored below). They show live account data.
automations/*/_probe_*.png
*.app/
# Build artifacts + Claude Code local state
build/
.claude/
Install-Recruiting-Report.command.zip
# Leader podium headshots — photos of real employees. The repo is PUBLIC, so
# these stay local and are synced to the mini through a private path, never
# committed. (Used by the Override/DD bulletin render.)
resources/leader-headshots/
# Per-run debug screenshots from uploaded automations - regenerated on
# every run; never useful to commit. Keep the directory itself tracked
# so the script can write into it on a fresh clone.
automations/uploaded/screenshots/*.png
# Shared-library scripts are materialized from the Google Sheet on each Hub —
# they're a local cache, not source. Never commit (would also block git pull).
automations/uploaded/_shared/
# Marks a DEV machine (Megan/Claude). When present, the launcher protects
# local edits (fast-forward-updates only when the tree is clean). When ABSENT
# (teammate machines), the launcher hard-aligns to origin/main every launch so
# a stray change or wrong branch can't strand them on stale code. Machine-
# specific — never commit (committing it would disable force-align for everyone).
.dev-machine
# Frontier OPT PDFs are uploaded daily sales data (customer info) — never
# commit. The script reads them from this directory at run time; cleanup
# is per-user.
automations/uploaded/frontier/
# Scratch probe scripts (_probe_*.py) under report modules are throwaway
# debugging from one-off mapping work — never commit. Keep them around
# locally if useful, but don't track them.
automations/*/_probe_*.py
# AppStream office list — machine-regenerated on every daily_focus run
# (refresh_offices_from_page scrapes the logged-in account's offices). It's a
# per-account runtime cache, not source. Tracking it dirtied the mini's tree
# after every run and blocked `lucy update` (git pull --ff-only). Readers
# (fill._load_office_index, dashboard._all_appstream_offices) fall back to an
# empty list if it's missing, so a fresh clone just rebuilds it on first run.
automations/recruiting_report/all-offices.json

# Per-machine runner identity for mini_control (Lucy 1 / Lucy 2). Never commit.
.machine-profile

# Streamlit secrets (never commit — contains access codes, SMTP + service-account creds)
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# swag_welcome: keep the raw personal handwriting sample + build debug art off the public repo
# (the derived glyph library IS committed, so the tool still works)
resources/swag/handwriting-raw.png
resources/swag/glyphs/_debug/

# ApplicantStream/Applicant Tracker Google service-account key (live private key,
# repo is PUBLIC) — distributed out-of-band, NEVER commit. Also the browser session.
applicant-tracker-service-account.json
applicant-tracker-service-account.json.bak.*
automations/applicant_tracker/service_account.json
automations/applicant_tracker/.browser_profile*
automations/applicant_tracker/downloads/
automations/applicant_tracker/.env

# Thread Builder runtime cache (regenerated from the Thread Plans sheet by
# thread_builder.sync; the sheet is the source of truth, not git).
automations/shared/thread_plans.json
output/thread_plans_store.json
# Blue Ink storage_state (blueink_docs) — live SESSION cookies for the
# alphaletemarketing@gmail.com account, which can SEND documents. The repo is
# PUBLIC. Never commit. Seeded by `python -m automations.blueink_docs.session
# --login` (a human logs in once; nothing types a password).
.blueink_storage_state.json
automations/blueink_docs/.blueink_storage_state.json
# ...and the persistent Chrome profile the --login seed writes. It holds the
# SAME live session (cookies for an account that can send legally-binding
# documents), and `git add <dir>` sweeps its thousands of files in without
# blinking — which is exactly what happened on 2026-08-24, caught before the
# commit. Wildcard so a _holder/_alt variant is covered too.
.blueink_profile*
automations/blueink_docs/.blueink_profile*

# Slack storage_state + profile (slack_skool_email) — live SESSION cookies for
# the AO workspace as a person who can invite people. The repo is PUBLIC:
# committing this hands a stranger that Slack session, which is worse than the
# invite link it exists to fetch. Same class as .blueink_storage_state.json
# above. Seeded by `python -m automations.slack_skool_email.slack_invite
# --login`; both spellings listed because the file is written next to the
# module, not at the repo root.
.slack_storage_state.json
automations/slack_skool_email/.slack_storage_state.json
.slack_profile*
automations/slack_skool_email/.slack_profile*

# The Slack + Skool links themselves live in slack-skool-creds.json, already
# covered by the *-creds.json* rule at the top.
.appstream_last_mint_attempt
